{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Let me lead on.</b> Like אתנהל עמם (\"I will lead on with them\")." "<b>At my pace.</b> The yod is superfluous, or it may be singular speech." "<b>According to the pace of the work.</b> On account of the livestock, which is my work and close to me, for the meaning of מלאכה is that which a person can do by his strength and under his authority; also property is called thus, as in אם לא שלח ידו במלאכת רעהו (Exodus 22:7). From this root is derived the word מלאך, because he is under the authority of the one who sends him. And לרגל is as in ויברך ד׳ אותך לרגלי (Genesis 30:30). It is also possible that לרגל is as it sounds: that he led them on their feet."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:46:55.748040128Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}